<div>
  <p>
    Brings a notification bell and friendly pop-ups into the Jenkins UI, so a pipeline can pause
    and ask a real person for input, get a generated file reviewed, or show off its numbers &#8212;
    instead of leaving it all buried in the console log.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>Ask a question</b> &#8212; the <code>askInteractive</code> step pauses a pipeline and asks
      someone to pick an option (or type an answer), right from the bell.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Review a file</b> &#8212; the <code>interactiveView</code> step publishes a generated file
      (a report, a plan, a diff, ...) for line-by-line comments and an approve / request changes /
      reject decision &#8212; like reviewing a document on Confluence.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Show the numbers</b> &#8212; the <code>interactiveOutput</code> step turns per-build stats
      (cost, carbon footprint, resource usage, ...) into KPI cards, a table, and trend charts on
      the build and job pages.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Answers can also come in automatically over a built-in web API, so a bot, script, or AI tool
    can respond on a person's behalf. Already using the built-in <code>input</code> step? An
    optional bridge can show those in the same bell too, with no changes to your existing
    pipelines.
  </p>
</div>
